<article class="env-lemma" id="09EX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09EX">Lemma <span data-tag="09EX">15.117.8</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring. Assume the reside field $\kappa _ A$ has characteristic $p > 0$ and that $a \in A$ is an element whose residue class in $\kappa _ A$ is not a $p$th power. Then $a$ is not a $p$th power in $K$ and the integral closure of $A$ in $K[a^{1/p}]$ is the ring $A[a^{1/p}]$ which is a discrete valuation ring weakly unramified over $A$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
